Package: kmod-keys-encrypted
Version: 6.12.44-r1
Depends: kernel (=6.12.44~f7f08650bddaa97c248fd5a463bd2380-r1), kmod-crypto-cbc, kmod-crypto-hmac, kmod-crypto-rng, kmod-crypto-sha256, kmod-keys-trusted
Source: feeds/base/kernel/linux
SourceName: kernel
License: GPL-2.0-only
LicenseFiles: COPYING
Section: kernel
SourceDateEpoch: 1750714327
Architecture: aarch64_generic
Installed-Size: 40960
Filename: kmod-keys-encrypted_6.12.44-r1_aarch64_generic.ipk
Size: 10160
SHA256sum: 01c87c2acdde3dd3c01290a4c420d280340a069d02d9dab8c40623407601b5ed
Description:  This module provides support for create/encrypting/decrypting keys
 in the kernel.  Encrypted keys are kernel generated random numbers,
 which are encrypted/decrypted with a 'master' symmetric key. The
 'master' key can be either a trusted-key or user-key type.
 Userspace only ever sees/stores encrypted blobs.

Package: kmod-keys-trusted
Version: 6.12.44-r1
Depends: kernel (=6.12.44~f7f08650bddaa97c248fd5a463bd2380-r1), kmod-crypto-hash, kmod-crypto-hmac, kmod-crypto-sha1, kmod-tpm
Source: feeds/base/kernel/linux
